{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the reason of <b>and it shall be that the firstborn whom she bears shall stand up in the name of his dead brother</b> is not according to its plain sense, that they would call the firstborn son by the name of the dead man — Reuben or Shimon like him — for concerning Boaz it is so stated (Ruth 4:10), 'and the name of the dead shall not be cut off from among his brethren and from the gate of his place,' yet they did not call him Mahlon. But this verse is, by way of truth, a promise, and behold it is like its plain sense. And our Sages relied upon it (Sifrei 256; Yevamot 24) as a midrash — that the eldest of the brothers should perform levirate marriage, and that the aylenit (a woman incapable of procreation) is not taken in levirate marriage, and likewise the wife of the saris (eunuch) whose condition is confirmed — but all of this is an asmakhta (scriptural support/hint), for the aylenit and the wife of the saris are derived from the body of the verse itself."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The word מָחוּי (makhui) in the phrase 'whose condition is confirmed' appears in some witnesses; it refers to the anatomical condition of the saris. I have rendered it descriptively rather than transliterating the technical term."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:55:34.002124063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}